    "status": "proposal - unverified against hardware",
    "target": "Cobber Mini Front (prodcode 4), forward-facing",
    "why_the_front_differs_from_the_rear": [
      "The rear crash mode is failure to DETECT you; attention capture wins.",
      "The front crash mode is failure to JUDGE YOUR APPROACH SPEED - a driver",
      "pulling out of a side road or turning across you is making a gap",
      "acceptance decision. Drivers read position, speed and direction from",
      "STEADY light; flashing degrades exactly the cue they need.",
      "A bicycle's narrow frontal profile already gives poor speed cues, so",
      "the steady component carries more weight here than at the rear."
    ],
